//images.unsplash.com/photo-1548013146-72479768bada?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1568605117036-5fe5e7bab0b7?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513694203232-719a280e022f?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80"], "shortInfo": "Anjar\n\nThe city ofAnjar\n\n was founded by Caliph Walid I at the beginning of the 8th century. The ruins reveal a very regular layout, reminiscent of the palace-cities of ancient times, and are a unique testimony to city planning under the Umayyads. "}, {"id": "hist_baalbek", "type": "historical", "name": {"en": "Baalbek", "bn": "Baalbek"}, "country": {"en": "Arab States", "bn": "Arab States"}, "subtitle": {"en": "UNESCO World Heritage • Arab States", "bn": "ইউনেস্কো বিশ্ব ঐতিহ্যবাহী স্থান • Arab States"}, "lat": 34.0071, "lng": 36.2049, "zoomAltitude": 0.14, "images": ["http://whc.unesco.org//uploads/thumbs/site_0294_0007-750-0-20110920201544.jpg", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544735716-392fe2489ffa?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1564507592333-c60657eea523?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1509023464722-18d996393ca8?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1552832230-c0197dd311b5?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1581888227599-779811939961?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1548013146-72479768bada?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1568605117036-5fe5e7bab0b7?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513694203232-719a280e022f?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80"], "shortInfo": "Baalbek\n\nThis Phoenician city, where a triad of deities was worshipped, was known as Heliopolis during the Hellenistic period. It retained its religious function during Roman times, when the sanctuary of the Heliopolitan Jupiter attracted thousands of pilgrims.Baalbek\n\n, with its colossal structures"}, {"id": "hist_burgos_cathedral", "type": "historical", "name": {"en": "Burgos Cathedral", "bn": "Burgos Cathedral"}, "country": {"en": "Europe and North America", "bn": "Europe and North America"}, "subtitle": {"en": "UNESCO World Heritage • Europe and North America", "bn": "ইউনেস্কো বিশ্ব ঐতিহ্যবাহী স্থান • Europe and North America"}, "lat": 42.3405, "lng": -3.7048, "zoomAltitude": 0.14, "images": ["http://whc.unesco.org//uploads/thumbs/site_0316_0011-750-0-20130221165152.jpg", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544735716-392fe2489ffa?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1564507592333-c60657eea523?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1509023464722-18d996393ca8?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1552832230-c0197dd311b5?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1581888227599-779811939961?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1548013146-72479768bada?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1568605117036-5fe5e7bab0b7?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513694203232-719a280e022f?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80"], "shortInfo": "Burgos Cathedral\n\nOur Lady of Burgos was begun in the 13th century at the same time as the great cathedrals of the Ile-de-France and was completed in the 15th and 16th centuries. The entire history of Gothic art is summed up in its superb architecture and its unique collection of works of art, inclu"}, {"id": "hist_byblos", "type": "historical", "name": {"en": "Byblos", "bn": "Byblos"}, "country": {"en": "Arab States", "bn": "Arab States"}, "subtitle": {"en": "UNESCO World Heritage • Arab States", "bn": "ইউনেস্কো বিশ্ব ঐতিহ্যবাহী স্থান • Arab States"}, "lat": 34.1192, "lng": 35.6475, "zoomAltitude": 0.14, "images": ["http://whc.unesco.org//uploads/thumbs/site_0295_0001-750-0-20110920200954.jpg", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544735716-392fe2489ffa?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1564507592333-c60657eea523?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1509023464722-18d996393ca8?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1552832230-c0197dd311b5?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1581888227599-779811939961?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1548013146-72479768bada?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1568605117036-5fe5e7bab0b7?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513694203232-719a280e022f?w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80"], "shortInfo": "Byblos\n\nThe ruins of many successive civilizations are found atByblos\n\n, one of the oldest Phoenician cities. Inhabited since Neolithic times, it has been closely linked to the legends and history of the Mediterranean region for thousands of years.Byblos\n\n is also directly associated with the histor"}, {"id": "hist_canadian_rocky_mountain_parks", "type": "historical", "name": {"en": "Canadian Rocky Mountain Parks", "bn": "Canadian Rocky Mountain Parks"}, "country": {"en": "Europe and North America", "bn": "Europe and North America"}, "subtitle": {"en": "UNESCO World Heritage • Europe and North America", "bn": "ইউনেস্কো বিশ্ব ঐতিহ্যবাহী স্থান • Europe and North America"}, "lat": 51.4247, "lng": -116.4797, "zoomAltitude": 0.14, "images": ["http://whc.unesco.org//uploads/thumbs/site_0304_0002-750-0-20121123104125.jpg", "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544735716-392fe2489ffa?w=1600&auto=form